VK: SwapChainBits::LATEST_READY prefers FIFO_LATEST_READY with VSYNC; features.latestReadySwapChain reports it.

SwapChainVK::Create maps "flags" on two preference lists. With VSYNC the list is FIFO_RELAXED (with
ALLOW_TEARING) or FIFO, then FIFO; without VSYNC it is MAILBOX (IMMEDIATE with ALLOW_TEARING),
then FIFO_LATEST_READY when VK_EXT_present_mode_fifo_latest_ready is supported, then FIFO. Where
MAILBOX is offered (always on NVIDIA) the FIFO_LATEST_READY entry hooked up in 50d103b is never
reached, and with VSYNC it is not in the list at all, so a caller that wants a vblank-paced
swap chain presenting the newest ready image has no way to ask for it. NRI doesn't report the
chosen present mode, so the caller can't find out either.

This adds SwapChainBits::LATEST_READY: with VSYNC, FIFO_LATEST_READY goes first in the capped
list when the device supports it, and the bit is dropped from the swap chain's flags unless that
mode was chosen. features.latestReadySwapChain reports the support (VK only; D3D11 and D3D12 drop
the bit, DXGI has no such mode). The uncapped list and every existing combination of flags
choose what they chose before. Measured on v190, NVIDIA (the surface offers FIFO_LATEST_READY and
MAILBOX): features.latestReadySwapChain = 1, a VSYNC | LATEST_READY swap chain creates and
presents with the Khronos layer clean; forcing the mode on a device without the feature gives
"presentMode is VK_PRESENT_MODE_FIFO_LATEST_READY_KHR, but feature presentModeFifoLatestReady is
not enabled".

diff --git a/Include/Extensions/NRISwapChain.h b/Include/Extensions/NRISwapChain.h
index 6097871..b6b1b35 100644
--- a/Include/Extensions/NRISwapChain.h
+++ b/Include/Extensions/NRISwapChain.h
@@ -49,7 +49,8 @@ NriBits(SwapChainBits, uint8_t,
     VSYNC               = NriBit(0), // cap framerate to the monitor refresh rate
     WAITABLE            = NriBit(1), // unlock "WaitForPresent" reducing latency (requires "features.waitableSwapChain")
     ALLOW_TEARING       = NriBit(2), // allow screen tearing if possible (METAL: "displaySyncEnabled = NO", may show partially rendered frames)
-    ALLOW_LOW_LATENCY   = NriBit(3)  // allow "NRILowLatency" functionality (requires "features.lowLatency")
+    ALLOW_LOW_LATENCY   = NriBit(3), // allow "NRILowLatency" functionality (requires "features.lowLatency")
+    LATEST_READY        = NriBit(4)  // VK: with "VSYNC" prefer "FIFO_LATEST_READY" (the newest ready image at vblank, no tearing) over "FIFO" (requires "features.latestReadySwapChain", ignored otherwise)
 );
 
 NriStruct(WindowsWindow) {  // Expects "WIN32" platform macro
diff --git a/Include/NRIDescs.h b/Include/NRIDescs.h
index 247960d..68ee4dd 100644
--- a/Include/NRIDescs.h
+++ b/Include/NRIDescs.h
@@ -2229,6 +2229,7 @@ NriStruct(DeviceDesc) {
         bool presentFromCompute;                                  // see "SwapChainDesc::queue"
         bool waitableSwapChain;                                   // see "SwapChainDesc::waitable"
         bool resizableSwapChain;                                  // swap chain can be resized without triggering an "OUT_OF_DATE" error
+        bool latestReadySwapChain;                                // see "SwapChainBits::LATEST_READY"
 
         // Multi view
         bool flexibleMultiview;                                   // see "Multiview::FLEXIBLE"
diff --git a/Source/D3D11/SwapChainD3D11.hpp b/Source/D3D11/SwapChainD3D11.hpp
index 16761da..81fe9e1 100644
--- a/Source/D3D11/SwapChainD3D11.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D11/SwapChainD3D11.hpp
@@ -164,6 +164,7 @@ Result SwapChainD3D11::Create(const SwapChainDesc& swapChainDesc) {
         m_Flags &= ~SwapChainBits::ALLOW_TEARING;
     if (!m_FrameLatencyWaitableObject)
         m_Flags &= ~SwapChainBits::WAITABLE;
+    m_Flags &= ~SwapChainBits::LATEST_READY; // DXGI has no such mode
 
     return Result::SUCCESS;
 }
